98
00:12:43,000 --> 00:12:50,000
systems. The infection rate is real, but the severity in healthy dogs is typically much lower than in humans

99
00:12:50,000 --> 00:12:57,000
facing the same exposure. Leptospirrosis is a bacterial infection transmitted through water contaminated with the

100
00:12:57,000 --> 00:13:04,000
urine of infected animals and it is a real threat to dogs. Dogs in areas with high wildlife populations and standing

101
00:13:04,000 --> 00:13:11,000
water are at meaningful risk. This is one of the cases where the dog's tolerance for contaminated water reaches

102
00:13:11,000 --> 00:13:18,000
its limits. Leptosperosis can cause severe illness and death in dogs which is why vaccination against it is

103
00:13:18,000 --> 00:13:22,000
standard veterinary practice in high-risisk areas.

104
00:13:22,000 --> 00:13:29,000
The dog is better than humans at handling contaminated water, but better is not the same as invulnerable. Heavy

105
00:13:29,000 --> 00:13:37,000
metals, chemical pollutants, and industrial contaminants represent a category where the dog's biological defenses provide essentially no

106
00:13:37,000 --> 00:13:44,000
advantage. The immune and digestive adaptations that handle microbial contamination are irrelevant to chemical

107
00:13:44,000 --> 00:13:52,000
toxins. A dog that drinks from water contaminated with heavy metals or agricultural chemicals faces the same toxicological risks as any mammal of

108
00:13:52,000 --> 00:14:02,000
similar size. Dogs impressive resistance to microbial contamination can create a false sense of security about chemical contamination that doesn't generalize.

109
00:14:02,000 --> 00:14:09,000
Cyanobacteria, blue green algae represent another significant limit case that deserves

110
00:14:09,000 --> 00:14:17,000
specific attention. warm, shallow, slowmoving water in summer conditions frequently produces blooms of

