00:16:14,000 --> 00:16:22,000
through travel, through a camping trip, through accidentally swallowing lake water, and the response is slow,

126
00:16:22,000 --> 00:16:31,000
non-specific, and more likely to result in illness than the response of an immune system that has encountered these organisms regularly. Dogs in outdoor

127
00:16:31,000 --> 00:16:40,000
environments maintain the continuous pathogen exposure that builds and sustains pathogen specific immune memory. In this specific respect, the

128
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:49,000
breadth and currency of microbial immune experience, the outdoor dog has a more comprehensively calibrated immune system for environmental pathogens than most

