00:20:56,000 --> 00:21:05,000
resistance. The incoming bacteria simply can't establish themselves in a community of organisms that is already occupying the available ecological

160
00:21:05,000 --> 00:21:13,000
space. And if anything does establish itself and begin to cause illness, an immune system with broad pathogen specific memory generated by previous

161
00:21:13,000 --> 00:21:21,000
exposure responds faster and more effectively than an immune system encountering the organism for the first time. The result is an animal that can

162
00:21:21,000 --> 00:21:29,000
drink from a parking lot puddle, absorb the microbial load it contains, and walk away fine. Not through magic or mystery,

163
00:21:29,000 --> 00:21:37,000
but through the accumulated adaptations of an evolutionary history spent in exactly those conditions. Your dog is

164
00:21:37,000 --> 00:21:43,000
not being reckless when it drinks from a puddle. It is operating within the parameters its biology was designed for.

165
00:21:43,000 --> 00:21:52,000
Its stomach acid, its mucosal immunity, its gut microbiome, its pathogen specific immune memory, all of it

166
00:21:52,000 --> 00:22:00,000
developed specifically to handle contaminated water. The puddle is not a threat to the dog. The puddle is, in a

167
00:22:00,000 --> 00:22:08,000
biological sense, the dog's natural habitat for hydration. You, by contrast, are the product of a water safety revolution that happened so recently in

168
00:22:08,000 --> 00:22:15,000
evolutionary terms that it's essentially invisible. Your body didn't evolve for treated water. It evolved for the same

169
00:22:15,000 --> 00:22:24,000
variable outdoor water that your dog is drinking from right now. The difference between you and the dog is not that the dog is robustly adapted and you are

